\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs22  
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (1\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 160\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) Reportatio in Codicis librum VI. Cap. 1, 1; Cap. 9, 1\endash 61, 8, 5a. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Incipit liber sextus de seruis fugitiuis et libertis mancipiisque\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Continua vt in glossa. {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Seruum. Ista lex diuiditur in tres partes}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 . In prima premissa maiorem imperator subuertit minorem \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22 . In secunda ponit consequenciam seu illacionem in tercia  ponit racionem illacionis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ...\endash ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Filiis autem. H\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [oc]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   d\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [icit]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   filius de proprietate aduenticii peculii nihil potest disponere ... respectu maiorum et parentum suorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 .\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash   Berufung auf\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Bar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tolus de Saxoferrato],\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Bal\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [dus de Ubaldis],\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Dy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [nus Mugellanus],\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Ja\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [cobus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  de Are\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tio], \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Vdalricus de Toma\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ,\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Johannes de Imola.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   \endash 161\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 170\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   leer;
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (171\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 194\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) Reportatio in Digestorum librum XXIV. Cap. 3, 1\endash 67. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Rubrica soluto matrimonio et quemadmodum dos petatur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Item nota quod prima continuacio rescriptatur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (?)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   a doc\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tore]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   et ab ea recedunt ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (171\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 )\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Dotis causa. Causa dotis priuilegiata est}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   propter fauorem r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [ei]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   p\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [ublicae]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   qui in liberis procreandis versatur ...\endash ... ut hic scribit Bar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tolus]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   in fi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [ne]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   verbis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (?);
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 198\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) Reportatio in Digestorum librum XXVIII. Cap. 3, 1\endash 19. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Rubrica de iniusto rupto et irrito \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  facto testamento\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Continua vt in glossa vel sic secundum Bar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tolum]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   videndum est supra de tes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tamento]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   vet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [eri]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   quia alium efficitur irritum alium dicitur iniustum etc. ... Testamentum. ...\endash ... \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [Lemma fehlt]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Si adoptetur institutus non est ... in persona primi morientis uel repudiantis, licet alius ad\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [h]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  uc uiuat et tamen non repudiauerit.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   \endash  199\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 200\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   leer;
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 (201\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 214\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) Reportatio in Digestorum librum XLIII. Cap. 1, 1\endash 11, 3. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Rubrica de interdictis et extraordinariis actionibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Continua vt hic in glossa et vide hic Dy\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [num]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   et Bar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tolum]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  ...{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[2].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17  Videamus. In hac lege igitur venio ad secundum}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   et quero quod \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (quot)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  sunt diuisiones interdictorum. Dic quod 4 sunt genera ...\endash ... vbi Bar\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [tolus]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   et Bal\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [dus] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  hoc declarant.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   \endash  214\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  -217\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   leer. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 Vgl. \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 A. Belloni\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 , Professori giuristi a Padova nel secolo XV. Profili bio-bibliografici e cattedre (Studien zur europ\u228 \'e4ischen Rechtsgeschichte 28) Frankfurt M. 1986 S. 157 (diese Hs.).}

