\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  13\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  \endash 17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22    {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\b\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Physiologus mit Begleitversen}}{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17   }}
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De vnicorni/ De incarnacione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[0].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Dicit philosophus vnicornis est animal pusillum}}\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Versus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 :\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   {\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://5650[1].5666l/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22\chcbpat17 Virgineis digitis capiendo sit hic fera mitis}}\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  / Qui mundum saluum facit intrat virginis aluum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   (\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs22 Henkel, \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  V. 3); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De leena/de resurreccione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Sequitur in philosopho cum leena peperit catulum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ... (V. 1); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De ydro/ De descensu ad inferos\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 4);\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De elephante/De baptismate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 9); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De onocentaurus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   (!) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  vecordes et bilingwes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 6); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De galadrio/ De saluandis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) (V. 19); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De panthera/ De redemcione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 2)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  ; \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De salamandra/ De iustis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 22); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De fenice/De ascensione\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 20);\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De aquila/De renouacione anime baptizate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) (V. 16); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Noctirax\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  / De perfidia iudeorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 18); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De syrena/ De uanitatibus seculi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 5); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De pellicano/ Christus viuificat nos lauacio\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  [ne]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   lateris sui\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (14\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) (V. 17);\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De aucula/ De detraccionibus et blasphemiis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 10); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De castore/De castitate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 15); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De ceruo/De penitencia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (15\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) (V. 12); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De onagero/ De temptacione dyaboli\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 8); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De capra/ Quod deus prouidit nobis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (V. 13); >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De serra alias de perseuerancia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  <  (V. 11);\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De volpi/ De dolosis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < (15\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) (V. 14) ...  (weiterhin ohne Verse); (17\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De basilisci \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  (!)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  /Penitencia dura\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   Basiliscus assimilatur peccato \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ...; \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  De tritimo/ De accidia etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22  < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Accidiosi sequuntur per piscem \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22 ...\endash ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  Sic isti seipsos et alios a bonis retrahunt de istis dicitur M\plain \f1\i\super\lang1033\fs24 t\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22   \plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   (23, 13) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs22  ve uobis qui clauditis etc.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs22   \endash  Hs. enth\u228 \'e4lt 41 Kapitel, davon 20 mit Begleitversen; sie erweist sich als gek\u252 \'fcrzte Bearbeitung der sogen. Dicta-Version. 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 
\par \pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs18 Druck der Dicta-Version nach Pierpont Morgan Library, New York Ms. 832, ehemals Stift G\u246 \'f6ttweig cod. ms. 39: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs18 G. Heider\plain \f1\lang1033\fs18 , Dicta Johannis Chrysostomi de naturis bestiarum, in: Archiv f\u252 \'fcr Kunde \u246 \'f6sterreichischer Geschichts-Quellen V (1850) S. 552\endash 582. \endash  Vgl.\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs18  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs18  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs18 N. Henkel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs18 , Studien zum Physiologus im Mittelalter (Hermaea NF 38) T\u252 \'fcbingen 1976 S. 29 f. ( Hs. genannt); Begleitverse gedruckt: \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs18 Henkel\plain \f1\lang1033\fs18  S. 44 ff.  \endash  \plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs16 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs18 VL VII 626 f.  ohne diese Hs. (Ch. Schr\u246 \'f6der).}

